<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Mach-O EXECUTABLES in the bundled engine payload of the
  Developer ID dmg (runtime/bin/python3.N, bin/odj-audio). Libraries carry none: macOS reads
  entitlements from the executable that starts the process, never from a
  dylib or extension module it loads.

  WHY. Open DJ's own analysis (librosa) runs numba, whose llvmlite JIT maps
  ordinary memory and then makes it executable. Under the hardened runtime,
  which notarization requires, that is refused and the kernel kills the
  process with SIGKILL, namespace CODESIGNING, "Invalid Page", faulting in
  LLVMPY_TryAllocateExecutableMemory. Measured Wed 16 Sep 2026 on demon-llama
  from the notarized build df075dda: every folder-import analysis run died
  with exit -9 four seconds in, and the unsigned payload verify had passed.

  WHY THIS KEY AND NOT allow-jit. allow-jit only covers memory mapped with
  MAP_JIT, which llvmlite does not use. Measured on silver the same day with
  the same Developer ID signed interpreter: allow-jit alone was still killed,
  allow-unsigned-executable-memory ran numba and librosa beat tracking.

  scripts/sign_macos_developer_id.sh applies this file and then runs a numba
  JIT under the signed interpreter, so a build that loses the key fails there
  rather than on a user's first import.

  WHY audio-input. Set recording (SET-10, SET-11) captures the REC input in
  bin/odj-audio itself, since the app bundles no ffmpeg. The hardened runtime
  refuses an audio input to any process whose own signature lacks this key,
  silently: the stream opens and delivers silence. The app's own copy
  (Entitlements.app.plist) does not cover a child executable. The signing
  script checks every executable carries it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
